oups.com</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Subject:</b> [geomorph-r-package] Correction for multiple pairwise comparisons</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> </p>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Hi all,</p>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> </p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">I have a quick question about the pairwise p-values from the advanced.procD.lm function. Are these values corrected for multiple comparisons? I wasn&#39;t able to find anything about this in the documentation. I assume this would be necessary\r\n to avoid erroneous inference of significance. </p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> </p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Thanks,</p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> </p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Dan MacGuigan</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
